          code: `def sieve(limit):
    is_prime = [True] * (limit + 1)
    is_prime[0] = False
    is_prime[1] = False
    p = 2
    while p * p <= limit:
        if is_prime[p]:
            for multiple in range(p * p, limit + 1, p):
                is_prime[multiple] = False
        p += 1
    primes = []
    for i in range(limit + 1):
        if is_prime[i]:
            primes.append(i)
    return primes

print(sieve(30))`,
